## Signature

- Provided by: **Qwen 3.8 Max (qwen/qwen-3.8-max)** — 2026-11-01
- Method: public internet research (**OpenAI `introducing-gpt-oss`** + **`openai/gpt-oss-120b` HF card** + **arXiv 2508.10925 "gpt-oss-120b & gpt-oss-20b Model Card"** — OpenAI ships **only two** weights: **gpt-oss-120b (116.8B/5.1B-active)** and **gpt-oss-20b (20.9B/3.6B)**; **no "120b-lite" checkpoint**; **Artificial Analysis `gpt-oss-120b-lite` → 404** (no independent measurement); **OpenCode Zen live catalog** — no `gpt-oss-*` "lite" route; **targeted web search for "gpt-oss-120b-lite"** returns **only this project's own `modelcomp.vercel.app` page** (circular, rejected as evidence). **Curated `meta`** — spec identical to the already-scored `gpt-oss-120b` (117B/5.1B MoE, 131,072 ctx, Apache-2.0, ~$0.15/$0.60), differing only by an unbenchmarked "concise reasoning" gloss.)
- Future sources: this becomes scoreable **only if** a **named, dated "gpt-oss-120b-lite" checkpoint** is published (OpenAI or a tracker) **with its own evaluation** demonstrably different from `gpt-oss-120b`. **Guards applied:** (1) do **NOT** transfer any **`gpt-oss-120b`** benchmark (AIME / SWE-bench Verified / GPQA / LiveCodeBench / MMLU-Pro / the 90.8% self-admitted hallucination) onto this label — that model is scored separately; (2) do **NOT** treat *"tuned for concise, high-density reasoning"* as a measured capability — no benchmark supports it; (3) reject the **self-referential modelcomp page** as independent corroboration; (4) **gpt-oss-20b** is also a different model, not this one. **No dimension scores are assigned.**
